<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_TarPitBelch.xml                    RM_TheSump · SUMP_TAR_BELCH_EVENT_1
  ============================================================================
  Owner ruling 2026-09-24, typed verbatim: "There should also occasionally be
  a random event when a tar pit just belches a huge amount of tar out all
  over the local terrain."

  SCOPE: this is the scenario-scoped v1. A later same-day ledger note on this
  item re-rules the belch's EVENTUAL shape as a FlowWorks flood pulse whose
  fronts cool to walkable glass, full rulings on SUMP_TAR_HYDROLOGY_1 — that
  item owns the whole canal-work/fire-network/Deep-Black-mere FlowWorks
  integration (none of it built yet: no pulse-spread or glass-cooling code
  exists on RM_Tar today). RUT_IncidentWorker_TarPitBelch.cs's own header
  carries the full reasoning; this def's trigger/anchor shape is meant to
  survive that later rebuild unchanged.

  workerClass finds an existing RM_TarDeep/RM_TarShallow cell on the map
  (LIQUID_TYPES_MOD_1's own generated tar-pit terrain, already real on Sump
  maps — SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1's own verify plan names "quicktest map with
  RM_TarShallow" as the reference) and splashes RM_Filth_Tar around it via
  RM_TarCoatingUtility (SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1 S1's already-shipped mechanism,
  which explicitly names this class as its intended first consumer).

  category Misc / allowedBiomes [RM_TheSump]: same shape RUT_Breaklight.xml
  already ships for a rare biome-restricted event — that header's own
  reasoning applies verbatim here (CanFireNow enforces allowedBiomes even off
  a Storyteller-driven roll, so baseChance is effectively "this biome's own
  share of the Misc queue"). baseChance 1 / minRefireDays 9 are this pass's
  own INVENTED-BUILD cadence — the owner said "occasionally," no number.

  MayRequire is load-bearing: workerClass resolves into
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards content (same posture RUT_TarMoat.xml and
  RUT_BeastBulge.xml already take for defs physically shipped inside this
  mod but depending on that shared assembly).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_TarPitBelch</defName>
    <label>tar pit belch</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_IncidentWorker_TarPitBelch</workerClass>
    <baseChance>1</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>9</minRefireDays>
    <allowedBiomes>
      <li>RM_TheSump</li>
    </allowedBiomes>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
